{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "51d43447-bb57-44de-bfc6-8c0d25af7318",
    "name": "EZ Key Encryption Keys admin",
    "description": "Collection for encryption key management and rotation operations in the Admin API.\n\n## Endpoints\n\n- **List Keys**: Get encryption keys (paginated)\n- **Get Primary Key**: Get current primary encryption key\n- **Get Key by ID**: Get specific encryption key details\n- **Rotate Key**: Manually trigger key rotation\n- **List Re-encryption Batches**: Get re-encryption batches (paginated; optional filters)\n- **Resume Batch**: Resume a failed or paused re-encryption batch\n- **Trigger Full Re-encryption**: Manually trigger full re-encryption process\n- **Trigger Re-encryption for Key**: Trigger re-encryption for a specific key\n- **Create Re-encryption Batches**: Create batches without processing\n\n## Authentication\n\nAll endpoints require admin authentication via Bearer token.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "4087"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "list keys",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response has content and page\", function () {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('content');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('page');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.content).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.page).to.have.property('totalElements');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.page).to.have.property('totalPages');",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    if (jsonData.content && jsonData.content.length > 0) {",
              "        pm.environment.set(\"encryptionKeyId\", jsonData.content[0].keyId);",
              "        var primaryKey = jsonData.content.find(k => k.keyStatus === 'PRIMARY');",
              "        if (primaryKey) {",
              "            pm.environment.set(\"primaryKeyId\", primaryKey.keyId);",
              "        }",
              "    }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys?page=0&size=20&sort=introducedAt,desc",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Zero-based page index"
            },
            {
              "key": "size",
              "value": "20",
              "description": "Page size"
            },
            {
              "key": "sort",
              "value": "introducedAt,desc",
              "description": "Sort (e.g. keyId,asc, keyStatus,desc)"
            },
            {
              "key": "keyStatus",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional filter: PRIMARY, ENABLED, DISABLED, PENDING",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns encryption keys with server-side pagination. Response has content (array of key objects) and page (size, number, totalElements, totalPages). Optional query param keyStatus filters by status."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "get primary key",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200 or 404\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"primaryKeyId\", jsonData.keyId);",
              "    pm.test(\"Key status is PRIMARY\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.keyStatus).to.equal('PRIMARY');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/primary",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "primary"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns the current primary encryption key used for new encryption operations. Returns 404 if no primary key is found."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "get key by ID",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200 or 404\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 404]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Key ID matches\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.keyId.toString()).to.equal(pm.environment.get('encryptionKeyId') || '{{encryptionKeyId}}');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/:keyId",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            ":keyId"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "keyId",
              "value": "{{encryptionKeyId}}",
              "description": "The encryption key ID"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns details for a specific encryption key by its ID. Use the keyId from the list keys response."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "rotate key",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200 or 500\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.environment.set(\"newPrimaryKeyId\", jsonData.newPrimaryKeyId);",
              "    pm.test(\"Rotation successful\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.newPrimaryKeyId).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.include('successfully');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/rotate",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "rotate"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "reason",
              "value": "{{reason}}",
              "description": "Audit justification for the manual key rotation (min 10 characters, recommended for SOC 2 CC8.1 compliance)",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Manually triggers encryption key rotation. This creates a new primary key and demotes the old primary key to ENABLED status. Useful for emergency rotations or testing. ⚠️ Use with caution in production."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "list re-encryption batches",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test(\"Response has content and page\", function () {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('content');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('page');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.content).to.be.an('array');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.page).to.have.property('totalElements');",
              "    pm.expect(jsonData.page).to.have.property('totalPages');",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    var rows = jsonData.content || [];",
              "    if (rows.length > 0) {",
              "        var failedBatch = rows.find(b => b.status === 'FAILED' || b.status === 'PAUSED');",
              "        if (failedBatch) {",
              "            pm.environment.set(\"reencryptionBatchId\", failedBatch.batchId);",
              "        }",
              "    }",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/reencryption-batches?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "reencryption-batches"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "page",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Zero-based page index"
            },
            {
              "key": "size",
              "value": "20",
              "description": "Page size"
            },
            {
              "key": "sort",
              "value": "createdAt,desc",
              "description": "Sort (e.g. batchId,asc, status,desc, targetTable)"
            },
            {
              "key": "status",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional: PENDING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, FAILED, PAUSED",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "targetTable",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional exact match on target table",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "targetColumn",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional exact match on target column",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "oldKeyId",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional filter on old key id",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "newKeyId",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional filter on new key id",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "createdAfter",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional inclusive lower bound on createdAt (ISO-8601)",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "createdBefore",
              "value": "",
              "description": "Optional inclusive upper bound on createdAt (ISO-8601)",
              "disabled": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns re-encryption batches with server-side pagination. Response has content (array) and page (size, number, totalElements, totalPages). Optional query params filter by status, target table/column, old/new key id, and createdAt range."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "resume batch",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 202, 404, or 500\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([202, 404, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 202) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Resume accepted\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.batchId).to.be.a('number');",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.be.a('string');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/reencryption-batches/:batchId/resume",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "reencryption-batches",
            ":batchId",
            "resume"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "batchId",
              "value": "{{reencryptionBatchId}}",
              "description": "The re-encryption batch ID"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Accepts resume for a failed or paused re-encryption batch (202 Accepted). Use the batchId from the list re-encryption batches response; progress appears in the batches table."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "trigger full re-encryption",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 202, 400, or 500\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([202, 400, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 202) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has batchesEnqueued\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('batchesEnqueued');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has batchIds\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('batchIds');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has message\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('message');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/reencrypt/trigger",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "reencrypt",
            "trigger"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Manually triggers full re-encryption: creates batches for all old keys and enqueues background processing. Returns 202 Accepted immediately; monitor progress in the re-encryption batches list."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "trigger re-encryption for key",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 202, 400, 404, or 500\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([202, 400, 404, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 202) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has keyId\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('keyId');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has batchesEnqueued\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('batchesEnqueued');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has message\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('message');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/:keyId/reencrypt",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            ":keyId",
            "reencrypt"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "keyId",
              "value": "{{encryptionKeyId}}",
              "description": "The old encryption key ID to re-encrypt (must not be PRIMARY)"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates and enqueues re-encryption batches for a specific old key (202 Accepted). The key must not be PRIMARY. Monitor progress in the batches list."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "create re-encryption batches",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"Status code is 200 or 500\", function () {",
              "    pm.expect([200, 500]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
              "});",
              "",
              "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
              "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has batchesCreated\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('batchesCreated');",
              "    });",
              "    pm.test(\"Response has message\", function () {",
              "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('message');",
              "    });",
              "}"
            ],
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "packages": {}
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url_admin_api}}/api/v1/encryption-keys/reencrypt/create-batches",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url_admin_api}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "encryption-keys",
            "reencrypt",
            "create-batches"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Creates re-encryption batches for all old keys without processing them. The batches will be processed by the scheduled job. Useful for preparing batches before scheduled processing or for testing batch creation logic."
      },
      "response": []
    }
